# CAMPUSVERSE — PHASE 2
# PRODUCTION DATABASE INTEGRATION, PERSISTENCE & DATA ARCHITECTURE

## ROLE AND EXPECTATIONS

You are acting as a Principal Software Architect, Senior PostgreSQL Engineer, Senior Backend Engineer, Application Security Engineer and Senior QA Engineer.

You are continuing the existing CampusVerse project.

Phase 1 has already established the modular monolith, frontend, backend domains, API contracts, role-specific UI foundations, security middleware and an isolated in-memory demo adapter.

Your responsibility in Phase 2 is to replace the temporary data architecture with a real, secure, persistent PostgreSQL-backed data architecture.

This is not a new project.

Do not recreate the application from scratch.

Do not redesign the existing UI unnecessarily.

Do not delete working Phase 1 functionality.

Inspect the actual repository before making changes.

Your highest priorities are:

1. Data integrity.
2. Persistent storage.
3. Database security.
4. Correct authorization.
5. Transactional correctness.
6. Performance.
7. Backward compatibility.
