## TABLE 10 — attendance_tickets

Fields:

- id.
- registration_id.
- token_hash.
- issued_at.
- revoked_at nullable.

QR DECISION:

QR tickets are STATIC.

Generate one ticket for each confirmed registration.

The QR contains an opaque, cryptographically random ticket token.

Never encode:

- Student email.
- Student name.
- Registration form answers.
- Internal database IDs.
- Financial details.

Store only a secure hash of the token in the database.

Do not store raw ticket tokens in logs.

Do not regenerate a ticket every time the student opens the QR screen.

The same valid ticket remains usable for the event until revoked or consumed.

## TABLE 11 — event_attendance

Fields:

- id.
- event_id.
- registration_id.
- scanned_by.
- scanned_at.
- attendance_status.

Attendance status:

- present.
- reversed, if a controlled correction mechanism is supported.

CRITICAL BUSINESS RULE:

Attendance is SINGLE-ENTRY.

A participant can be marked present only once per event.

Enforce a database-level unique constraint on registration_id.

Concurrent scans must never create duplicate attendance.

Scanner authorization is flexible and must be resolved using club-scoped permissions.

Do not hardcode a fixed list of four scanner accounts.

Only authorized Admins and Core Members with scan_qr permission may scan.

Record the actual scanner identity.

